  "term": "systematic approach",
  "definition": "A systematic approach is an organized, step-by-step way of handling a task so that methods are applied in a planned sequence and the results are checked for reliability. In the source, it means combining several analytical methods, comparing their performance, and using the best-supported model for the final decision.",
